 is what the LORD of Armies says: ‘Consider your ways."},{"verse":8,"text":"Go up to the mountain, bring wood, and build the house. I will take pleasure in it, and I will be glorified,” says the LORD."},{"verse":9,"text":"“You looked for much, and, behold, it came to little; and when you brought it home, I blew it away. Why?” says the LORD of Armies, “Because of my house that lies waste, while each of you is busy with his own house."},{"verse":10,"text":"Therefore for your sake the heavens withhold the dew, and the earth withholds its fruit."},{"verse":11,"text":"I called for a drought on the land, on the mountains, on the grain, on the new wine, on the oil, on that which the ground produces, on men, on livestock, and on all the labor of the hands.”"},{"verse":12,"text":"Then Zerubbabel the son of Shealtiel and Joshua the son of Jehozadak, the high priest, with all the remnant of the people, obeyed the LORD their God’s voice, and the words of Haggai the prophet, as the LORD their God had sent him; and the people feared the LORD."},{"verse":13,"text":"Then Haggai, the LORD’s messenger, spoke the LORD’s message to the people, saying, “I am with you,” says the LORD."},{"verse":14,"text":"The LORD stirred up the spirit of Zerubbabel the son of Shealtiel, governor of Judah, and the spirit of Joshua the son of Jehozadak, the high priest, and the spirit of all the remnant of the people; and they came and worked on the house of the LORD of Armies, their God,"},{"verse":15,"text":"in the twenty-fourth day of the month, in the sixth month, in the second year of Darius the king."}],"hasArtwork":true,"artworkUrl":"/data/images/books/haggai.svg","availableLangs":["en","zh-CN"]},{"id":"haggai_2","bookSlug":"haggai","chapter":2,"reference":"Haggai 2","title":"Haggai 2 — Public Domain Study","topics":["haggai","haggai","ot","scripture","哈該書","哈该书","新殿的榮耀","新殿的荣耀"],"snippet":{"en":"In the seventh month, in the twenty-first day of the month, the LORD’s word came by Haggai the prophet